## Setup and render

Requires Quarto, a working LaTeX installation, and Make. Install the project-local [coatless-quarto/assign](https://github.com/coatless-quarto/assign) extension once (and commit `_extensions/` for reproducibility):

```sh
make setup
make exams            # assignment, solution, grading PDFs
make exams-assign
make exams-solution
make exams-grading
```

Output goes to `_output/assignment`, `_output/solution`, and `_output/grading`. This is a **default document project**, not a website.

Author the exam in `exam.qmd`. Copier creates one numbered file per question (`tasks/task_1.qmd`, `tasks/task_2.qmd`, and so on), and `exam.qmd` includes each corresponding file. Each task can contain common text and `:::{.direction}`, `:::{.sol}`, and `:::{.rubric}` sections; the extension selects the content for each profile. Keep points in `exam.qmd`, not in reusable tasks. The cover sheet lives in `partials/before-body.tex` and is shown only in the assignment profile.

The total score is divided into integer question scores automatically. Every question receives `total points // number of questions`, and any remainder is added one point at a time to the first questions. The generated headings and cover-sheet scoring table use the same calculation. If you manually change the question structure after generation, update both `exam.qmd` and `partials/before-body.tex` together.

